From 5eab74b9227eb99cfe3dad43cd99ae1429e64d62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Manuel de Brito Fontes <aledbf@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 21:53:46 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] ftrace: Skip the weak function scan when sorttable has
 run

Since commit ef378c3b8233 ("scripts/sorttable: Zero out weak functions
in mcount_loc table"), sorttable zeroes the __mcount_loc entries of
overridden weak functions when CONFIG_BUILDTIME_MCOUNT_SORT is set,
and ftrace_process_locs() skips the zeroed entries. Yet
ftrace_check_for_weak_functions() still queues a scan of every record
through kallsyms_lookup() at boot, and ftrace_check_sync() waits for it
at late_initcall_sync, although there is nothing left for it to find.

Return early from ftrace_check_for_weak_functions() when
CONFIG_BUILDTIME_MCOUNT_SORT is set. Module records are still checked
in ftrace_module_enable(), as sorttable does not process modules.

On an x86_64 KVM guest with one vCPU the scan is 11.9 ms of a kworker's
CPU during boot, and on that vCPU it runs inside acpi_init(). Together
with the previous patch, the time from kernel start to "Freeing unused
kernel image" goes from 110.0 ms to 89.5 ms (p50 of 15 boots,
interleaved), and available_filter_functions lists no
__ftrace_invalid_address__ entries.

The trade-off: an entry sorttable failed to zero would no longer be
disabled at boot, and would be listed as __ftrace_invalid_address__.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 kernel/trace/ftrace.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/trace/ftrace.c b/kernel/trace/ftrace.c
index db8eeaefe..d8a55f6ad 100644
--- a/kernel/trace/ftrace.c
+++ b/kernel/trace/ftrace.c
@@ -4405,6 +4405,14 @@ static __init void ftrace_check_work_func(struct work_struct *work)
 
 static int __init ftrace_check_for_weak_functions(void)
 {
+	/*
+	 * sorttable zeroes the mcount entries of overridden weak functions at build
+	 * time, and ftrace_process_locs() skips what it zeroed: there is nothing left
+	 * for this scan of every record through kallsyms to find.
+	 */
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_BUILDTIME_MCOUNT_SORT))
+		return 0;
+
 	INIT_WORK(&ftrace_check_work, ftrace_check_work_func);
 
 	ftrace_check_wq = alloc_workqueue("ftrace_check_wq", WQ_UNBOUND, 0);
-- 
